                        ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
                    }
                    DESCRIPTION ""
                }
                ^"Shift Human Shapes" DEF {
                    PROPERTIES {
                        ^"Cost" STRING "1 point"
                        ^"Initiative" STRING "0"
                        ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
                    }
                    DESCRIPTION "Allows the knight, who is usually armored to demonstrate his role, to remove the armor simply by thinking about it."
                }
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Combat footnote: * Does not include +3 to Attack and Defense for being mounted. Soak +9*: Faerie metal scale, made of glamor using the Shift Human Shapes Power. Pretenses footnote: Many knights have far higher scores than this. These statistics are correct for faeries that plan to improve their Pretenses by losing to a character, then mirroring his experience gain for the season. Equipment: Arms and armor. Has a faerie horse constructed of the knight's own glamor, so it flies when the knight does, and shares the knight's Magic Resistance. Courtier as squire. These faeries are often encountered outside courts, on lonely roads, and guarding bridges. They seek out defeat by humans as a way of gaining additional combat Pretenses. They are never seen with their armor off, so they may be a role that other faeries take on when they wish to enjoy some blood sport. Faerie Knights are more bound to the rules of chivalry than real knights, and so they do not use the Damaging Effect Power on their weapons against worthy foes."
            REFERENCES {
                "Magic Resistance" -> #tmM1uJVBdvXpEsg4iImNPyjr ^"Magic Resistance"
                "Damaging Effect" -> #t885Vlj2jC9rqq8xEP0AI5tP ^"Damaging Effect"
            }
        }

